---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Glance: Look at Another Tab Over Your Page | Blanc Browser"
  description="Open another tab as a card over your page with Blanc Glance. Move and resize it, keep using the page behind, or open it as a tab or a split."
  path="/features/glance"
  page="feature-glance"
  current="features"
  ogImage="/feature-glance.png"
  ogImageAlt="A Glance card floating over a page in the signed Blanc app, with its Change, Open as tab and Keep as split controls."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline slot="head">
{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://blanc.day/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Features","item":"https://blanc.day/features"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Glance","item":"https://blanc.day/features/glance"}]}
  </script>
<main id="main-content" class="feature-page feature-detail-page">
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/features">features</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">glance</span></nav>
  <section class="feature-hero feature-hero--detail feature-hero--text" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
    <h1 id="glance-title">Look at another tab without leaving your page.</h1>
    <p>Glance opens another open tab as a card over the page you’re on, and the page behind stays usable.</p>
  </section>
  <figure class="product-capture feature-capture released-capture">
    <a href="/feature-captures/glance-v1.40.0.png" aria-label="View full Glance capture"><img src="/feature-captures/glance-v1.40.0.webp" width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="A Lisbon travel guide in a Glance card floating over a map of Lisbon, in the signed Blanc app." /></a>
    <figcaption>The card floats over your page. You choose the tab it shows.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <section class="feature-copy-grid feature-copy-grid--top" aria-labelledby="glance-section-0">
    <div><h2 id="glance-section-0">Bring another open tab into view.</h2></div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list">
      <article><h3>Choose explicitly</h3><p>Press ⌘⇧G on macOS or Ctrl+Shift+G on Windows and Linux, or choose View → Open Glance. Pick a tab from the current window; the picker stays within its local profile.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Put it where you want it</h3><p>Drag the card’s header to move it, or an edge to resize it, or use the arrow keys on its Move or resize control. Double-click the header to put it back. Blanc remembers where you left it on this device.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Change, open, or finish</h3><p>Use Change to choose another tab, Open as tab to make it the current tab, or Keep as split to show the two side by side in Split View. Close Glance, or press Escape on its header, without closing either tab.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="glance-section-1">
    <div><h2 id="glance-section-1">A temporary view for the task in front of you.</h2></div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list">
      <article><h3>Both visible pages stay available</h3><p>Selecting a quiet tab for Glance reloads it. While it is open in Glance, Quiet Tabs leaves it alone. The page behind the card stays usable, and switching to another tab closes Glance.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Keep the choice local</h3><p>The picker uses tabs from this window and profile. It does not search history, Favorites, remote tabs, or another window.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <aside class="truth-note" aria-labelledby="glance-note-title">
    <h2 id="glance-note-title">Glance is temporary.</h2>
    <p>Glance is never written to session restore or sync. Only the card’s size and place are remembered, on this device. The underlying ordinary tabs keep their usual browsing behavior.</p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/features/tab-groups" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="glance" data-cta-position="related-feature">Keep related tabs in Named Groups <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </aside>
  <section class="feature-close" aria-labelledby="glance-close-title">
    <h2 id="glance-close-title">Make room for the way you browse.</h2>
    <a class="cta" href="/download" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="glance" data-cta-position="feature-close">download blanc</a>
  </section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
